"""v2 train-only GPU re-encode (owner G22-OWNER-ACK, delegated relay 2026-10-05T21:40Z; L6 caps).

Standalone (stdlib + numpy + torch + psutil) so one file runs on xbabe1/xbabe2/xbabe3 under /usr/bin/python3.12. The
pinned pretrained forwards are Codex's `gpu_encoders.Encoders` (sha256 ff419384..., the #199 runtime source), imported
read-only from ENC_ROOT; their models are checked against the pins before any CUDA work. Nothing here writes to S3 or to
ENC_ROOT: outputs go to --out, and are published later from xbabe2 through the guarded v2 writer (tools/v2_publish.py).

Per plan row (one published clean context): the encoder JTT1 bytes are verified (gz and raw sha256 equal the published
manifest's), and only the outer-train block is decoded (train_view slices the bytes before any parse). Exact/affine
copies of the target are dropped train-only, as in the v1 worker. Then hyperion(X), foundation(X, y), target(X, y),
tabpfn35(X, y) run on CUDA, and context2048 is assembled from hyperion, foundation and target with the pinned transforms.
Each output is the pooled float32 vector saved as <component>.npy; context.json copies the parent identity, lists the files
and carries a `gpu` block per component (recipe digest, seconds, peak memory, GPU UUID, input binding).

Budget (L6): a per-host append-only ledger (fsynced) records an intent before and a result after every component run;
at most 2 attempts per (view_id, component), a per-host GPU-second cap (default 8 h, so 3 hosts <= 24 h), and the
2026-10-10T00:00Z deadline. Unknown outcomes (intent without result) count as attempts.

Admission (PLAN 6.8, read-only): no foreign CUDA compute app on this GPU; >= 20 GiB free at start; the intake
tabpfn-gpu.lock is checked in /proc/locks by inode and never opened for locking; CPU instant < 95% and rolling < 85%;
the lane cpu-admission guard where present. Not admitted -> wait 15 s; more than 20 min -> exit YIELDED (manual relaunch).

--pilot K runs the leak pilot on the first K plan rows instead of production: each context is encoded (a) as is, (b) with
the outer-test byte block overwritten (train_view must be byte-identical and outputs bit-identical), and (c) a must-fail
control that deliberately appends the outer-test rows to X (its outputs must differ). Pilot GPU time is charged.

HYPERION-V6ALL (owner HYPERION-V6-ALL-NOW, 2026-10-06): optional component hyperion_v6all = the v6all fine-tuned weights in
the same pinned architecture and v5 recipe, selected exactly like hyperion_v6 (--components ...,hyperion_v6all
--hyperion-v6all PATH#SHA256). It is bound on the Encoders instance in Runner.__init__ and reached through Runner.one's
generic component call, so jtt1_header/train_view/drop_target_copies/Runner.encode/Runner.one are byte-identical to the
previous version and every existing component's code path and output bytes are unchanged.

Usage: v2_gpu_encode.py --plan PLAN.jsonl --out DIR [--pilot K] [--host-cap-hours 8] [--limit N]
"""
